u _\Omega . \end{equation} We call the classes of smooth real $(1,1)$-forms modulo $\mathrm{dd}^{\mathrm{c}}C^\infty (X,\mathbb R)$ background classes . By proposition 12.4.1 , the form $\mathfrak g_	heta $ descends to background classes of directions and is positive definite there. A change of representative of $	heta $ leaves its solution form $\Omega $ unchanged, and a change of representative of a direction is absorbed by the derivative of the solution potential. Thus $\mathfrak g$ is intrinsically defined on the background classes in $\mathscr P$. On every finite-dimensional affine family whose directions are linearly independent modulo smooth $\mathrm{dd}^{\mathrm{c}}$ terms, it is a smooth Riemannian metric. These variations change the background class. Directions obtained by varying a potential inside one fixed class are exactly the directions annihilated by ( 12.4.4 ). Thus this construction concerns a different space from the potential-space geometry of section 11.2 .

